---
import BaseLayout from "../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import PageHero from "../../components/PageHero.astro";
---
<BaseLayout title="An order is an order. Wherever it starts." description="Bring website checkouts, WhatsApp requests and walk-in sales into one order workflow.">
<PageHero eyebrow="The Kora product plan" title="An order is an order. Wherever it starts." lede="Bring website checkouts, WhatsApp requests and walk-in sales into one order workflow." />
<section class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-4 py-14 prose-kora">
<h2>Start with the right variant</h2>
<p>Black trainers in size 43 are a different stock item from size 42. An order saves the selected SKU, quantity, agreed price and customer details.</p>
<h2>Reserve before promising</h2>
<p>The backend checks available stock when the order is committed. A draft or customer enquiry does not automatically remove stock. Confirmed orders can hold units for a defined period.</p>
<h2>Keep payment and fulfilment separate</h2>
<p>An order can be awaiting payment, paid but not collected, partially fulfilled or completed. Those are different events, with different effects on inventory.</p>
<h2>Build the channels in stages</h2>
<p>The MVP starts with merchant-created and counter orders. A connected storefront and official WhatsApp assistant will reuse those same backend operations. AI-assisted extraction must ask about unclear items rather than inventing prices or quantities.</p>
<p><a href="/pilot" class="btn btn-primary">Explore the founding pilot</a></p>
</section>
</BaseLayout>
